# Testing Best Practices

## Testing Strategy

- Write tests for critical business logic
- Test user interactions and workflows
- Test edge cases and error scenarios
- Mock external dependencies (Supabase, APIs)
- Test accessibility requirements
- Maintain high test coverage for utilities and hooks

## Unit Testing

- Test individual functions and components in isolation
- Use Jest for unit tests
- Mock dependencies with jest.mock()
- Test pure functions thoroughly
- Test custom hooks with @testing-library/react-hooks
- Keep tests focused and simple

## Component Testing

- Use React Testing Library for component tests
- Test user behavior, not implementation details
- Query elements by accessible roles and labels
- Test user interactions (click, type, submit)
- Test loading and error states
- Avoid testing internal component state

## Integration Testing

- Test complete user flows
- Test interaction between multiple components
- Test with realistic data
- Mock only external dependencies
- Test authentication flows
- Test form submissions end-to-end

## Mocking Supabase

- Mock Supabase client in tests
- Create mock data factories
- Mock authentication state
- Mock database queries and responses
- Test error scenarios from Supabase
- Use consistent mock data across tests

## Testing Patterns

- Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- Use descriptive test names
- One assertion per test (when possible)
- Test the happy path first
- Then test edge cases and errors
- Clean up after tests (cleanup in afterEach)

## Server Actions Testing

- Test Server Actions in isolation
- Mock Supabase server client
- Test validation logic thoroughly
- Test authentication checks
- Test error handling
- Mock revalidatePath and revalidateTag

## API Route Testing

- Test API routes with mock requests
- Test all HTTP methods
- Test request validation
- Test authentication and authorization
- Test error responses
- Test response formats

## Testing Hooks

- Use @testing-library/react-hooks
- Test hook state changes
- Test hook side effects
- Test error scenarios
- Test with different props
- Clean up subscriptions

## Testing Forms

- Test form submission
- Test validation errors
- Test loading states
- Test success scenarios
- Test accessibility
- Test keyboard navigation

## Accessibility Testing

- Use jest-axe for automated a11y testing
- Test keyboard navigation
- Test screen reader labels
- Test ARIA attributes
- Test focus management
- Test color contrast

## Snapshot Testing

- Use snapshots sparingly
- Review snapshot changes carefully
- Don't snapshot large components
- Update snapshots intentionally
- Use for stable UI components
- Avoid for dynamic content

## Test Coverage

- Aim for high coverage on critical paths
- 80%+ coverage for utilities and helpers
- Don't chase 100% coverage blindly
- Focus on meaningful tests
- Use coverage reports to find gaps
- Test business logic thoroughly

## Performance Testing

- Test component render performance
- Test memo effectiveness
- Identify expensive re-renders
- Use React DevTools Profiler
- Test with realistic data sizes
- Optimize slow tests

## E2E Testing (Optional)

- Use Playwright for E2E tests
- Test critical user journeys
- Test on multiple browsers
- Test authentication flows
- Test with real Supabase instance (test project)
- Run E2E tests in CI/CD

## Best Practices

- Write tests alongside code
- Run tests before commits
- Keep tests fast
- Use test-driven development when appropriate
- Refactor tests like production code
- Maintain test utilities and helpers
- Use TypeScript in tests
- Document complex test setups
